  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Since impostors do not use conventional geometry, anything you try to project onto them with a projector component is likely to look very very wrong. Especially in club/rave worlds that may project effects onto players and where it is very likely that instances are performance gated (therefore lots of impostors), you'd end up seeing big weird glowing planes around the impostors. To avoid visual artifacts, I think it'd be better to make them ignore projectors entirely. That would just require a single added tag in the shader:\n\nTags\n\n{\n\n\"IgnoreProjector\" = \"True\"\n\n}",
